Here is the commit message:
SOLR-5231: Fixed a bug with the behavior of BoolField that
 caused documents w/o a value for the field to act as if the value were true
 in functions if no other documents in the same index segment had a value of
 true.

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/dev/trunk@1521948 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the default behavior of the `BoolField` implementation, where documents without a value for the field were treated as if their value was true when there were no other documents in the same index segment with a true value. This was due to the ordinal mapping logic in `BoolFieldSource`, which initialized the true ordinal (`tord`) to -1, leading to incorrect evaluations in function queries.

